15	// The people on the active sheet, in the order they were added, and the form that adds a person
16	// or, once a person's editor is opened, saves changes to them. Each person's row lists their claims
17	// and shows what they have claimed (their OPEN and SETTLED claims) and what is due on it: the sum of
18	// those claims' due figures; the sheet's
19	// claimed-total and due-total add up everyone's (a due-total that is n/a is skipped). A statement
20	// taken of a person binds each of their counting claims to the figure it shows then; the row shows
21	// how many statements they have had and the last one's due-total and date. A person can be retired
22	// from a date; retired people are left out of the list unless "show retired" is on, but their claims
23	// keep counting in every total. A person can be put on hold and taken off it again: while held,
24	// their OPEN claims count in no live total (theirs, the sheet's or a period's); SETTLED ones still do.
25	// A claim is due by its date plus the sheet's terms; an OPEN one due by a date before the sheet's
26	// today is overdue. Each row, and the sheet, shows how many of the claims that count are overdue and
27	// what is due on them. An overdue claim's due gains the sheet's late percent of its figure for every
28	// full 30 days it is overdue; a statement never binds that charge, settling fixes it in.
29	// A person can name other people on the sheet as their patrons, one at a time from their row; the
30	// row shows their patrons' names, sorted, and their backing: their patrons' due-totals added up
31	// (a due-total that is n/a is skipped).
